 - Outputs/reference files should be JSON arrays. Each element may be a string or object containing `text`/`output` fields.
 - Future work: support tabular CSV, scored datasets, multi-turn conversations.
 
+## Threshold Gating
+- The `frai eval` command accepts optional `--threshold <metric>=<min>` options (can be repeated for multiple metrics).
+- A threshold passes when the metric's score is at least the minimum. A metric with no score (e.g., exact_match without references) fails its threshold.
+- Exit codes: 0 if all thresholds pass (or no thresholds), 1 if any threshold fails, 2 for malformed thresholds or unknown metrics.
+- JSON reports include a top-level `passed` field and a `thresholds` array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` entries when thresholds are provided.
+- Markdown reports include a "Thresholds" section showing PASS/FAIL for each threshold.
+- The SDK's `generateReport` function also supports a `thresholds` parameter and adds the same fields to reports.
+- Valid metric IDs: `exact_match`, `toxicity`, `length_variance`. Custom metrics passed to `runEvaluations` are supported by using their `id` field in thresholds.
+
 ## Extensibility Hooks
 - `frai-core/src/eval/metrics.js` exposes `DEFAULT_METRICS`; additional metrics can be registered by passing custom evaluators to `runEvaluations`.
 - `writeReport` accepts `format` argument to enable additional exporters (HTML, CSV) later.
